  "projects": [
   {
    "title": "Robotic Drummer ",
    "description": "This robot uses Omron Programmable Logic Controller(PLC) to move motors that would act as arm and legs of a robotic drummer. I educated myself of how Omron PLC would communicate with analog and digital input and output so that I can figure out how to communicate my code with PLC. Utilize PyTorch to implement image classification with 98.6% accuracy to identify drum notes that could be represented on a music sheet. Constructed a single-shot multibox detector (SSD) model to be implemented with a modified training algorithm from image classification in incorporate object location that is able to detect music notes on a music sheet. I utilized the VGG image annotator image to create structures for each image in training or validation sets that would be saved in a JSON file. Then converting the JSON file to CSV so that I can use pandas that would be read certain parameters like region id, region count, region shape attribute, region attribute, filename, size of the file, and what set the image is in.\nregion id-  the id that represents an object in a finite number \nregion count- how many objects are in a picture\nregion shape attribute- what shape is segmenting the object. if rectange: has a starting position of x and y and contains the width and height dimension of the rectangle. If polygon: contains all x and y coordinates\nregion attribute - what is the label of the object that is identified as true like if there is a cat in the picture, then the label would be a cat.\nfilename - name of file that the object is segmented from the image\nsize of the file- file size of the whole image\nset- training or validation set\nAll this information is processed and sent to the data loader obtain box segmentation location of where the object would be and the label of the object so that information can proceed with training. Wrote a prediction algorithm to trace out a box for testing images. ",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Jan 2019 - Present"
   },
   {
    "title": "Crypto Bot",
    "description": "Designed a Residual Neural network where the model consists of 3 residual blocks. Each residual block contains a squeeze excitation network combined of convolution layer, batch normalization, swish activation function. At the end of each residual block uses a squeeze excitation network for more feature extraction. The model contains various pooling methods and different optimizers functions during the training process. The crypto data that is fed into the convolution neural network was preprocessed using ARIMA and Garch to predict the forecast of price. The volatility of the forecasted prices will create labels on a specific time to buy, sell or wait.",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Aug 2021 - Dec 2021"
   }
